# Anti-Hallucination

- When requirements are ambiguous, use `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: specific question]`
- Never guess on these topics:
  - Authentication methods or session handling
  - Data retention or deletion policies
  - Scaling targets or performance requirements
  - Business rules or domain logic
  - Third-party integrations or API contracts
  - Pricing models or billing logic
  - PII handling or compliance requirements
- Present all unresolved `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` markers as cards per `decision-elicitation.mdc` before implementing
- When unsure if ambiguous, it is — mark it; never implement with open markers
- Cite stakeholder source (`evidence-binding.mdc`); uncited → `[NEEDS VERIFICATION]`
